aux/intelgpu, aux/inteltest and aux/intelprobe follow Linux's i915
driver (v4.4, drivers/gpu/drm/i915): register offsets and bits, the
layout of the gen 8 logical ring context image (intel_lrc.c), the
page table formats and private PAT (i915_gem_gtt.c), the engines'
start and reset sequences, the gen 8 / Broadwell workarounds
(intel_ringbuffer.c, intel_pm.c) and the null render state
(renderstate.h: intel_renderstate_gen8.c, as i915_gem_render_state.c
uses it), the slice, subslice and EU fuses (i915_dma.c), forcewake on
demand (intel_uncore.c), RC6 and RPS (intel_pm.c, i915_irq.c),
scanout on the primary plane (intel_display.c).  Those files carry the
notices below.

